# This suite reads credentials via cy.env('WIKI_USERNAME') / cy.env('WIKI_PASSWORD')
# (see cypress/utils/env.js) - only needed to run cypress/e2e/external/**;
# the default stable suite needs no credentials at all.
#
# There are two equivalent ways to provide them locally; pick one.
#
# Option A - cypress.env.json (gitignored, used for local runs):
#   Run `npm run setup:env` to create it from cypress.env.example.json,
#   then fill in a disposable test account. See SECURITY.md.
#
# Option B - OS environment variables (used in CI). Cypress auto-picks up any
# variable prefixed with CYPRESS_ and strips the prefix, so:
CYPRESS_WIKI_USERNAME=your-test-account-username
CYPRESS_WIKI_PASSWORD=your-test-account-password
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit real credentials. Use a disposable Wikipedia test
# account created solely for this suite, not a personal or production account.
# See SECURITY.md for details.
